### Current Behavior

`10.42.7.0/24` not auto approved by this acl config:

```json
{
  "autoApprovers": {
    "routes": {
      "10.42.0.0/16": [
        "k8s"
      ]
}
```

when use this, it work:

```json
{
  "autoApprovers": {
    "routes": {
      "10.42.7.0/24": [
        "k8s"
      ]
}
```

### Expected Behavior

`10.42.7.0/24` auto approved by this acl config:

```json
{
  "autoApprovers": {
    "routes": {
      "10.42.0.0/16": [
        "k8s"
      ]
}
```

### Steps To Reproduce

use this acl config to test `10.42.7.0/24` :

```json
{
  "autoApprovers": {
    "routes": {
      "10.42.0.0/16": [
        "k8s"
      ]
}
```

### Environment

```markdown
- OS: Ubuntu 22.04
- Headscale version: v0.23.0-beta2
- Tailscale version: 1.68.2
```


### Runtime environment

- [ ] Headscale is behind a (reverse) proxy
- [ ] Headscale runs in a container

